#
# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for a machine that draws with lavapipe, added
# to tsan.supp's own: tools/drive/bare_driver.py sends the machine both, as
# one file, and stress.py hands this desk's rounds both the same way, now
# that a move to another renderer tears a lavapipe device down with its
# instance here too (seen on Ubuntu's Mesa 26.0.8: the same two races, in
# lp_fence_destroy() by the debug info, which GCC's symbolizer does not
# read from Ubuntu's .dwz-split package, so the frames stay unnamed).
#
# ---- lavapipe's device thread ----------------------------------------------
# Checked against the x11-vulkan-bare round on Debian 13's Mesa 25.0.7: two
# races, pthread_mutex_destroy against pthread_mutex_lock and
# pthread_cond_destroy against pthread_cond_broadcast, on one heap block that
# a thread vkCreateDevice spawns allocated. Every frame is in
# libvulkan_lvp.so; ours appear only as the callers of vkCreateInstance and
# vkCreateDevice.
#
# Keyed on the destroys, for tsan.supp's reason: the innermost frame is
# TSan's interceptor, and Debian's lavapipe has no symbols to key on below
# it. `race:libvulkan_lvp.so` is not the narrower form -- it matches any
# stack through the driver, which is where a race on a mapped buffer of ours
# would be. These do also cover src/core/thread.h's own destroys, wherever
# lavapipe is installed: the cost of keying on TSan's interceptor.
#
# And on the Raspberry Pi 4 they cover two of V3DV's (Mesa 26.2.5, Arch
# Linux ARM), checked against a KMS run there with no suppressions: the
# same pair, pthread_mutex_destroy and pthread_cond_destroy at
# vkDestroySwapchainKHR against pthread_mutex_lock on a thread the driver
# started from vkQueuePresentKHR, on the swapchain's own block, every
# frame in libvulkan_broadcom.so -- Mesa's display WSI, whose thread waits
# on the DRM descriptor, and whatever orders it against the destroy is out
# of TSan's sight. The Pi gets them as a lavapipe machine; one with V3DV
# and no lavapipe would want them of its own.
race_top:pthread_mutex_destroy
race_top:pthread_cond_destroy
